    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d292">

                <pb facs="0332" n="326" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg326"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/18521: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-14T17:00:00+01:00">January 14, 1942—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 14—4:09 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. Helsinki’s 32, January 12, 3 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d292-f1"/> German
                    propaganda concerning Soviet plans for border states also having noticeable
                    effect in Sweden where fear and distrust of Russian aims is scarcely less than
                    in Finland. British Minister<anchor n="2" xml:id="d292-f2"/> has telegraphed his
                    Government suggesting some statement be made by Mr. Eden<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d292-f3"/> in House of Commons which would allay apprehensions of
                    the northern countries and that Soviets be pressed to make some disavowal of
                    aggressive intentions. Should our Government find it possible publicly to make
                    some <pb facs="0333" n="327" xml:id="pg327"/> contribution to the same end,
                    would have immense value in strengthening support here for cause of democracies
                    in Government and public opinion.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Helsinki.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
